{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From shortness of spirit and from hard labor</b> — not because they did not believe in HaShem and in His prophet, but rather they did not incline their ear to his words <b>from shortness of spirit</b> — like a person whose spirit grows short in his toil, and who does not wish to live another moment in his suffering, even though he knows that he will find relief afterward. And the shortness of spirit is their fear — lest Pharaoh kill them by the sword, as their taskmasters said to Moses — and the hard labor is the pressure under which the taskmasters pressed them and would not let them pause to hear a matter and reflect upon it:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:38.695783944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}